The best interval we can use (the interval whose points are given that's closest to $x=-9$) is the interval between $x=-10$ and $x=-7$. Let's find the average rate of change between those points.

$\begin{align}
g'(-9)&\approx\dfrac{g(-7)-g(-10)}{-7-(-10)}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{-33-(-35)}{3}
\\\\
&\approx0.67
\end{align}$
